    "abstract": "Illustrated parts figure for the main landing gear leg assembly, showing the two lower torque link clamps that correspond to the plated and the sprayed sliding tube coating standards, the second listed as an alternate rather than as a replacement.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the main landing gear leg assembly, the torque link clamps, the side stay attachment hardware and the sensor installations, for one leg.",
      "figure_note": "The leg is shown extended with the doors removed. Items 30 and 30A are the two lower torque link clamps and each corresponds to a sliding tube coating standard; the sprayed coating builds up on the running surface and needs the thinner clamp. The clamp for the sprayed standard is listed as an alternate and does not supersede the clamp for the plated standard, so a station may keep ordering against the plated item until the plating line stock is exhausted. The sensor kit at item 50 is deleted at the first overhaul after the coating change and is shown for identification only. Left and right legs are handed at the side stay lug and share every other part number."
    },
